# Agent coordination

- Before writing, identify the exact Git root, file scope, active agents and
  uncommitted overlap. One repository has at most one active writer.
- Prefer the available direct agent or task channel. Send four short fields:
  task, files/area, what and why, and the next potentially conflicting action.
- `/kom <agent-or-task> <message>` invokes the project skill `kom` and means:
  contact that existing agent now, then report whether the message was sent.
- Do not create a new agent merely to satisfy `/kom`. Ask Jakob if no intended
  recipient can be identified safely.
- If direct messaging is unavailable, write a secret-free temporary note under
  `.agents/coordination/<agent-id>.md` and tell the user that delivery is not
  live. Remove or mark it complete when ownership ends.
- On overlap, pause the overlapping edit and agree on ownership, ordering or a
  compatible split. Never overwrite, stage, commit or rewrite another agent's
  work without agreement.
- Use repository authority, typed contracts and tests when one option is
  clearly stronger. Ask Jakob when materially different options remain about
  equally defensible or change security, data, product scope or cloud state.
